INT. COLD STORAGE WAREHOUSE, LOADING DOCK - NIGHT

Frost on steel. Fog from the freezer doors. A forklift idles with its lights on. Pallets of boxed fish stacked to the ceiling.

VALENTIN MOROZOV, 40s, in a parka, checks a manifest. CORINNE ABBOTT, 30s, in a black ski jacket, stands beside a pallet, tapping a tablet. MATEUS SOARES, 30s, a forklift driver in a reflective vest, leans on a pole. HANA PARK, 20s, a nervous clerk, clutches a clipboard.

He glances at his watch. She glances at him.

He whispers to the clerk. She goes pale.

                    CORINNE
          Something wrong?

                    VALENTIN
          Paperwork.

A truck horn sounds outside. He signals to the driver. The driver nods.

Mateus climbs onto the forklift. Hana steps back.

                    HANA
          Mr. Soares, that pallet isn't on the list.

                    MATEUS
          It's on mine.

He lifts the pallet. A box slips. It splits on the concrete, and ice-wrapped bricks of white powder spill out.

Silence. Valentin's hand goes to his jacket.

Corinne looks at the powder. She looks at him. She steps in front of Hana.

                    CORINNE
          Hana. Behind me.

Valentin draws. She raises her tablet like a shield. He fires. The tablet shatters. She dives, rolls, and kicks the forklift's emergency stop.

Mateus tumbles from the seat. Hana screams. The lights flicker.

He scrambles toward a pallet. Valentin pursues him through the stacked boxes.

She grabs Hana's wrist and drags her toward the dock door. A shot rings. Plaster dust rains.

At the door, she rips it open. Cold night air rushes in. Red and blue lights flash across the lot. Sirens rise.

Valentin stops in the middle of the aisle. He lowers his gun slowly, looking at the lights.
